From c7e618ea6d9e8c474eb43dd35c024a056c2531b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:19:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync links-diff: settle window, so sync lag
 is in_flight and only persistent differences are unclean

Why (live proof t_01a1d5c12a26ef3f, laptop-1, core 9c459c5d43, 2026-11-13): `hermes kanban sync links-diff`
never reported clean: True. Every sample (6, 20 s apart) listed 1-3 brand-new cards (ids minted in the last
~2 min, mostly chat 20261026_170127_f07c32) in only_in_ledger or only_in_replica, each gone within 20-60 s. The
diff is one raw snapshot of two stores that propagate asynchronously (origin ledger vs Board replicas), so on a
gateway whose chats spawn cards all the time clean is False nearly always and cannot serve as a parity gate.

Fix: new hermes_cli/kanban_chat_links_settle.py. links_diff(..., settle_s, poll_s) re-reads the raw snapshot
(_links_snapshot, the old links_diff body, unchanged) every poll_s (default 2 x kanban.sync.interval_seconds,
at least 5 s) for up to settle_s, and keeps as a difference only an entry EVERY read lists (unreadable boards
too). Entries that cleared, or appeared only in a later read, go to a new `in_flight` section and do not make
the report unclean. It stops at the first read in which nothing of the first read persists, so a quiet or
converging board answers in one or two reads; a persistent divergence (the old hub t_d3e3f88a shape) is read
through the whole window and stays clean: False. The CLI settles by default (90 s: above the slowest observed
lag, ~60 s) and gains `--settle SECONDS` (0 = one raw read, the old behaviour); the text output prints the
in_flight counts. links_diff() with no settle_s is the raw snapshot, so existing callers/tests are unchanged.

Proof:
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_chat_links_settle.py (10 tests): a fresh card the replica gets within the
  window is in_flight and the report clean (2 reads); a persistent ledger-only link stays unclean through
  the whole window with the lag beside it in in_flight; entries only a later read lists, entries that clear
  and come back, only_in_replica, unreadable replicas, the capped last sleep, the poll default, and the CLI
  default / --settle 0 / text output.
- 14 source mutants (sdlc-review mutants.py: each intersection, the early stop, unreadable handling, sleep
  cap, poll floor/fallback, settle 0 raw path, poll_s passthrough, CLI default/flag/printing): 14 killed.
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_chat_links{,_profile_board_pins,_owner_hub_subs,_released}.py pass.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: health ok.
